%% Approved WorkPM Option A: preserve fork history with local upstream merges.
%% The parent checkout may remain dirty; unrelated root changes are never rewritten.
flowchart TD
  Start([Begin approved Option A]) --> Inventory[Record parent and nested state; preserve unrelated dirty root changes]
  Inventory --> Snapshot[Capture baseline SHAs and rollback refs]
  Snapshot --> Worktrees[[Create disposable study and integration worktrees]]
  Worktrees --> Fetch[Fetch live upstream tips into disposable worktrees]
  Fetch --> PdsMerge[Merge atproto permissioned-data-alpha into the PDS fork]
  PdsMerge --> PdsConflict{PDS merge conflict?}
  PdsConflict -->|No| ClientMerge[Merge current social-app main into the client fork]
  PdsConflict -->|Yes| PdsResolve[Resolve only PDS integration conflicts and inspect generated output]
  PdsResolve --> ClientMerge
  ClientMerge --> ClientConflict{Client conflict set remains?}
  ClientConflict -->|No| Generated[Regenerate generated files and refresh dependencies from source]
  ClientConflict -->|Yes| ClientResolve[Resolve package, session, login, feed, settings, and translation hotspots]
  ClientResolve --> Generated
  Generated --> Boundary[Verify Spaces data plane and Radlib policy boundary remain separated]
  Boundary --> Pins[Update nested gitlinks, upstream pins, baseline, and rebase receipt]
  Pins --> Verify[Run fast, focused, contract, unit, typecheck, build, and PDS gates]
  Verify --> Gates{All required local gates pass?}
  Gates -->|No| Rollback([Discard candidate worktrees or restore prior local refs; record failure])
  Gates -->|Yes| Canonical{Push or default-branch change authorized?}
  Canonical -->|No| LocalDone([Complete local synchronization only])
  Canonical -->|Yes| OutOfScope([Stop and request separate authorization])
